{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510550-is-this-an-annoying-character","id":1510550,"title":"Is this an annoying character?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-02T20:29:42-07:00","id":1510550,"title":"Is this an annoying character?","content":"So I was playing werewolf 20th online with a big group of people, and I made a character I thought was really fun, and I know some others also thought it was super fun. However, apparently some people complained behind the scenes to the person running thing, saying they thought the character was really disruptive. It is a group thing, and I don't want to cause headaches for the dm, so I just made a different character and moved on. However, since I did that, I never actual spoke to any of the people who complained, and I was wondering if I could get people's opinions here. Just to see their thoughts on it.<br /> <br /> She was a galliard glass walker, and was kind of like a ditzy valley girl type, who was spoiled by rich parents. She always wears high heels and dresses every where, and occasionally talks about weird and slightly silly stuff(like wanting a Frappuccino machine in the caern, or talking about her plushie collection), and she has a lot of money so throws it around. So I am aware it isn't a like a stereotypical character but she is a glass walker, and the game takes place in LA. Also as a galliard I feel it is more okay to be a bit more 'flamboyant'. So I feel like it is within the standard of people with some experience in the game might do, to spice things up a little. Like I didn't make a clown or anything, there are actually people like that.<br /> <br /> I don't know, what do other people think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T20:40:00-07:00","id":1510551,"title":"","content":"I think personal preference and execution is going to matter here. I can see where you were going, and I can see how it could be a good character, but I can see it easily being grating if not done right.<br /> <br /> I think something here is that, even as a Glass Walker, you haven't really described her strengths as a Garou. What's she actually doing for her Sept and Pack? How does she contribute to the war against the Wyrm? A lot of WtA players, IME of course, will happily put up with some strange characters as long as it's clear that the character is a positive addition to things. If they never see how the character is working towards the cause, and all they see are the entitled ditzy stuff, they're less likely to take the PC well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T20:52:29-07:00","id":1510553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510550-is-this-an-annoying-character?p=1510551#post1510551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think personal preference and execution is going to matter here. I can see where you were going, and I can see how it could be a good character, but I can see it easily being grating if not done right.<br /> <br /> I think something here is that, even as a Glass Walker, you haven't really described her strengths as a Garou. What's she actually doing for her Sept and Pack? How does she contribute to the war against the Wyrm? A lot of WtA players, IME of course, will happily put up with some strange characters as long as it's clear that the character is a positive addition to things. If they never see how the character is working towards the cause, and all they see are the entitled ditzy stuff, they're less likely to take the PC well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel someone should mention Elle Woods as a good example of what you're getting at, so here's that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T21:02:20-07:00","id":1510555,"title":"","content":"I didn't really list the positives, since they never really came out in the game. People complained right away from the start before ever really learning much about her. It is certainly plausible that they just looked at the surface level stuff, judged her useless, and then complained without giving her a chance. I admit, I kind of took for granted people would give it a few games to get to know a character before actually complaining that the character is disruptive. So you think that might be it?<br /> <br /> For the record, she is a face type(high socials) and uses social media to influence humans. I am sure it came across she was really pretty and gets a lot of attention online and stuff, though it might not have clicked for people just how powerful she was at, at influencing humans. We didn't get into a fight during that time either, but she is actually a beast in combat as well. She definitely doesn't look like it however.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T21:08:50-07:00","id":1510556,"title":"","content":"Being an outsider to it, it's hard to say, but I've been in a lot of &quot;big online&quot; style games since they became a thing, and I've definitely seen a lot of prejudging of characters that weren't given a chance to show what they can contribute to the game before people were complaining.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm guilty of prejudging plenty myself, but I'd never complain to the ST(s) without giving the character a chance to defy my read of the surface.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T21:47:08-07:00","id":1510557,"title":"","content":"I feel like an outsider and I was playing the game. That character by far, got like the most compliments of any character I have played, and a lot of people were saying they thought it was a really cool concept and liked the character, thought it was fresh and unique. So I was really shocked when I heard a bunch of people had complained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T21:55:11-07:00","id":1510560,"title":"","content":"What is this character's motivation anyway, it's good that she can be useful, but I, without wanting to be boring, I can't see what reason she would have to join the fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T22:08:25-07:00","id":1510561,"title":"","content":"She wants to save the planet. It is kind of like how green is trendy now, and it is stylish to recycle and promote green energy, and the younger generation really cares about the earth. That is like her surface level, but she is also a garou so wanting the protect the planet goes far deeper than that. At the end of the day, she is just genuinely a good person that really does care about saving the planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T22:16:21-07:00","id":1510563,"title":"","content":"Okay... it's kind of a character... I think it's functional, just maybe too nice based on what you said. How were the other players characters? What can you say about then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T22:42:06-07:00","id":1510564,"title":"","content":"Well there is a pretty good mix of people, mostly glass walkers, gnawers, and children of gaia. She might be the most 'bubbly' type character, but there are other people who act silly, and there is even one person I know who is icly annoying on purpose. So while she does stand out in some ways, it isn't like I am playing her in an all combat game or anything. A more combat focused character might fit in a little better, but as far as I know, no one complained about any of the other people who didn't fit into that.<br /> <br /> She might be too nice, I could kind of see that, but would several people really complain about it right away?\u200b It is WoD, so maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T23:24:34-07:00","id":1510568,"title":"","content":"In the end, the ST allowed the character in. If her sheet and her backstory all showed what sort of person she was, it is on the ST to have denied her if she did not fit in.<br /> <br /> Don't bother with the ones that complain about her, I'd say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T07:16:52-07:00","id":1510592,"title":"","content":"This is just a guess based on what you've told me and my own experience. If there really wasn't a very big problem with your character, I think some of them either found it offensive/dangerous in some way or already had bad experiences with a character, maybe not similar, but with a very different concept and that's why they didn't want to play with it, (for several reasons) but didn't know how to approach you without hurting you or didn't want to be branded as villains and risk a fight so they spoke directly to ST alone to avoid the worst case scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T07:37:45-07:00","id":1510596,"title":"","content":"What is the character's take on being a tale-keeper? Because that's what the elders are going to expect her to be doing as a Galliard. Does her grasp of social media play into it? And have their been any Veil-endangering selfies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T09:04:29-07:00","id":1510606,"title":"","content":"Well she was really good at singing and dancing and stuff, and I imagine she would tell tales in an entertaining way, like a performer or actor. I am not sure how social media would really play into it, since obviously you can't post about garou stuff online(and she didn't). Though they share similar skills. She was a really young character, and I only played her for a very short time, so that was a work in progress. You can't plan every single thing before even playing the game though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T13:01:31-07:00","id":1510625,"title":"","content":"So from this thread, it honestly sounds like there isn't any issue with the character itself. The main take away I get, is that if you are playing a character that is a bit more unusual, you got to ease into it a little bit, otherwise might spook some people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T13:41:39-07:00","id":1510633,"title":"","content":"At least with a larger play group, yeah, it's usually better to start with a more &quot;conventional&quot; concept so people get to know you, and see that you &quot;get&quot; the game before you start playing around too much with concepts that explore more edge-case stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T15:00:10-07:00","id":1510641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lilitha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510550-is-this-an-annoying-character?p=1510606#post1510606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well she was really good at singing and dancing and stuff, and I imagine she would tell tales in an entertaining way, like a performer or actor. I am not sure how social media would really play into it, since obviously you can't post about garou stuff online(and she didn't). Though they share similar skills. She was a really young character, and I only played her for a very short time, so that was a work in progress. You can't plan every single thing before even playing the game though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, this is useful, you can use this to expose information directly on the network and sabotage some member of Pentex; can organize a march to use as a distraction while another group invades a protected location or even as cover, after all a group of Garou in human form can stay hidden inside a march; you can use it as a spy, each of her followers has a life and a cell phone, if she needs an eye or an ear in the right corner one of her followers can arrange it; they must have all kinds of jobs, the ST can use information that one of them has to start an adventure or use it as a hook, or even you can use it to enter places you normally wouldn't go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T22:48:24-07:00","id":1511108,"title":"","content":"telling people you want a Frappuccino machine in the caern? I assume you mean sept, right? The Caern is the most sacred space werewolves have. Asking for one in the Caern is like asking to fuck over the coffin during a funeral. \u200bEven for a glass walker, that's too far. <br /> <br /> <br /> Did you account for the realities of being a werewolf-soldier? Like, I'd think the consumerism would be beaten out of you, or maybe made something you feel guilty of. Wearing high-heels as a werewolf? In certain contexts, maybe, but usually a hard-no. Maybe the Valley girl might be something you might switch on, but all the time? no.<br /> <br /> Should a social primary really be so grating? I know, I know, it's hard to RP 5 charisma, appearance, intelligence, wits and expression when in reality you're just a 4 in these things, but some behaviours are best avoided. Even if you've got an idea of what to imitate, at high charisma you should maybe minimise some of the negative characteristics. On the otherhand, sometimes when you're playing a charismatic asshole, some players are going to be driven to hate you, not just for your actions but by the stats you don't have IRL that say you get away with it. If someone's being a dick but the ST tells everyone that he's likeable or magnetic, that's much more frustrating than just dickery.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T23:08:31-07:00","id":1511109,"title":"","content":"The Sept is a social unit, the Caern is the physical space. The <b>Heart</b> of the Caern is the only part where even Glass Walkers would find a lack of solemnity exceedingly inappropriate. Most Glass Walker Septs probably have a nice cafe somewhere on the Caern's Bawn as it is. This is just a logical extension of how most Septs build dining amenities in the Bawn to cook up feasts for Caern Rites that either require them or are celebrated with them (The Moot Rite itself being a prime example): you want those things in places that are secured from the outside world, not beyond the Bawn in the Sept's larger Protectorate where the Veil needs to be enforced even if Garou and Kin have worked hard to have a strong control over it.<br /> <br /> Also the Glass Walkers tend not to &quot;beat&quot; consumerism out of their members. One of the Revised signature characters is a Homid Glass Walker Theurge who's regularly depicted in a business suit with heels.. and nobody - at least within the Tribe - gives her shit about it.<br /> <br /> Lastly, it's the ST's game. If the valley girl GW Galliard is a fit in the ST's interpretation of the setting, it's not our place to question that. The OP didn't say that there was any problems from IC conflicts stemming from the character's behaviors, but OoC conflicts because people were talking shit behind backs about the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T02:03:21-07:00","id":1511112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510550-is-this-an-annoying-character?p=1511108#post1511108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">telling people you want a Frappuccino machine in the caern? I assume you mean sept, right? The Caern is the most sacred space werewolves have. Asking for one in the Caern is like asking to fuck over the coffin during a funeral. \u200bEven for a glass walker, that's too far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the Caern, a mixed Caern might have problems with that. But Urban Caerns for Glass Walkers are detailed in the tribebook and the Book of the City - they seem to have all the conveniences of life, and while no one would place something like that in the Heart of a GW Caern (it's after all reserved for the spirit of the Caern and/or the Cockroach pit) there is bound to be all kinds of amneties in the sorrounding areas. If the Caern totem itself was a spirit of beauty or a spirit of social media, I could actually see it favouring Instagram/Twitter style influencers and their quirks and consumerist tendencies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510550-is-this-an-annoying-character?p=1511108#post1511108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you account for the realities of being a werewolf-soldier? Like, I'd think the consumerism would be beaten out of you, or maybe made something you feel guilty of. Wearing high-heels as a werewolf? In certain contexts, maybe, but usually a hard-no. Maybe the Valley girl might be something you might switch on, but all the time? no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it, though? The Signature Glass Walker Theurge in Revised is walking around in stilletos, power suits and slinky night out dresses. In the Glass Walker writeup, she's in Glabro, in her glitzy top and miniskirt, taking off her heels. I think you're underestimating how much the Glass Walkers enjoy being human.\u200b<br /> <br /> Also when your totems are the City Fathers, Al'Mighty Dolla and Easy Credit you're not going to have all that many problems with this.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's a not even a question if it's a valid concept for a Glass Walker, or Glass Walkers in general, the only questions are how they were portrayed and is it a Sept they would work in.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T03:17:51-07:00","id":1511115,"title":"","content":"Oh 100% I'm on board with Valley-girl glass walkers, but 100% you'll need to modify it to make it work. <br /> Glass walkers were always a tribe of characters other garou may find iffy if not downright sacrilegious, surrounding themselves with the comforts of the weaver and doing weird shit like dying their fur green or fixing metis flaws with works that belong in science-fiction. <br /> <br /> But...<br /> I expect a Garou consumer to be a socially conscious. They might not necessarily agree with every flag you could wave, but propagating harmful archetypes isn't great. Let's also not skip over the influence your elders will have in educating you to be part of Garou society. <br /> <br /> Given the stress of the regular monster-murders garou go on, a ditzy personality seems like a coping mechanism. When you regularly put your life on the line, spoiled-brat stuff just seems egregious. The Valley girl stock character originated from upper-middle class women and later those who love conspicuous consumption and didn't really care for achievements; I suspect being able to behave like that is the result of being sheltered and privileged, but like... are Garou privileged that way? Garou culture is violent and heavily geared towards personal achievements in the form of honour, glory and wisdom, the pavlov's dog or WTA. Galliards don't need honour but neither glory nor wisdom mesh with this kind of behaviour. Some other breeds might get renown for having all the shineys but not Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T13:14:49-07:00","id":1511150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1510550-is-this-an-annoying-character?p=1511115#post1511115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh 100% I'm on board with Valley-girl glass walkers, but 100% you'll need to modify it to make it work.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) If you're 100% on board with the valley-girl GW, then the idea that you 100% have to modify it makes no sense.<br /> 2) None of what you're saying is actually addressing the OP's character as related to us, or the situation as related to us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I expect a Garou consumer to be a socially conscious. </div> </div> </div>The PC was already explained to be an online influencer type that used that reach to sway human consumption. That business requires at least looking the part in public because being caught not following your own advice is a great way to tank as an influencer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's also not skip over the influence your elders will have in educating you to be part of Garou society. </div> </div> </div>Let's not skip that Mentor is a discouraged Background for Glass Walkers (and formerly a <b>banned</b> one before discouraged was added to the game) because GW traditions are designed specifically to diminish the power of Elders to stop young Garou with new ideas from flourishing. It's one of the Tribe's biggest saving graces: they actively avoid stifling the next generation (it's why their name has changed three times), and actually provide lots of material support thanks to all of that Weaver-loving stuff they do so young GWs can actually do things in new arenas of the battle against the Wyrm as they crop up instead of trying to figure out how to fight in a new space and raise the resources to do it at the same time.<br /> <br /> GWs, because of their status as an urban primary Tribe, don't leave education of cubs and Cliaths to Elders. They have specialists that have proven track records in on-boarding new Garou quickly because living in the city doesn't leave them time to slowly indoctrinate fresh Garou into how thing work. Even GW raised by kin-in-the-know still need rapid response education: they have(/had) lives in human society that will notice if they're missing for too long. They need to not break the Veil, but exist with human (and digital) eyes all around them.<br /> <br /> GW Elders need to peddle their own influence later after GW education teams do their jobs, by offering support for initiatives new GWs come up with, rather than expecting to just toss their Rank around from the get go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suspect being able to behave like that is the result of being sheltered and privileged, but like... are Garou privileged that way? </div> </div> </div>According to the material on both the Silver Fangs and Glass Walkers? The ones that want their families to be can make sure that's that case, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Garou culture is violent and heavily geared towards personal achievements in the form of honour, glory and wisdom, the pavlov's dog or WTA. Galliards don't need honour but neither glory nor wisdom mesh with this kind of behaviour. </div> </div> </div>1) The books explicitly state that Renown is generally considered by pack, no individual, behavior. Being the distraction that lures a fomori into an Ahroun's teeth gets the same Renown despite not delivering the killing blow. It's specifically geared to group achievements, not personal ones.<br /> 2) Galliards are screwed over by the Renown charts regardless of other character quirks. If it wasn't for packs getting Renown as a group, Galliards would be unplayable in group play because they'd be vastly behind everyone else that can get lots of renown just doing their archetypal Auspice stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}